<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0-windows</TargetFramework>
    <UseWPF>true</UseWPF>
    <PackageId>MindAttic.Components.Wpf</PackageId>
    <!-- HOUSE-LAW-1: whole-number versions only; bump the major. -->
    <Version>23.0.0</Version>
    <Description>Shared WPF theme (dark chrome palette, tool/text button, pin toggle, themed
      dropdown menu styles), a DropdownMenu control (a themed, pinnable action menu that closes
      its own popup before invoking an action, so it's never on screen for a screenshot or the
      start of a recording), and an AddressBar control: a themed Back/Forward/Reload(/Home) +
      URL bar attachable to a CoreWebView2 that can change at runtime, with an optional
      navigation guard a host can use to veto any action. MaWindow.DarkTitleBar asks Windows to
      draw a window's title bar dark to match the theme. MaModal is an in-window modal dialog
      (dimmed backdrop, themed card with a heading, close button and footer) opened through a
      bindable IsOpen, closed by Esc or a backdrop click, with focus trapped inside and returned
      on close. MaProgressBar styles a ProgressBar as a thin rounded track with a coloured fill,
      determinate or indeterminate. MaBadge is a small outlined pill (an optional icon-font glyph
      and a word in a state colour) with a plain MaTag variant for a type or category label.
      Building blocks: MaPillChoice (a single-choice pill row), MaPillToggle, MaCard,
      MaStatCard/MaSmallStat tiles, the MaFocusRing keyboard focus ring, MaHeading/MaSectionLabel/
      MaMutedText text styles, and MaLineChart, a themed percent-over-time line chart (time and
      percent axes, reference lines, per-point segment colours, a dotted projection).
      MaToast is a themed notification card (accent stripe, a title and two-line body
      that is one clickable button, a dismiss button), and MaToastHost a row that stacks them
      from a bound collection and announces each new one politely to screen readers.
      MaHyperlink styles a Hyperlink in text: the MaLink accent, SemiBold, underlined only on hover
      and keyboard focus.
      MaTextBox.Placeholder shows muted placeholder text in an empty MaTextBox, and MaTextArea is
      the multi-line text box whose thin themed scroll bars show when its text overflows.
      MaMessageBox.Show is a themed stand-in for MessageBox (a dark-title-bar window with an icon,
      the message and OK / OK-Cancel / Yes-No / Yes-No-Cancel buttons, returning MessageBoxResult)
      for prompts when no app window is open to host an MaModal.
      MaSpinner is a busy ring in MaAccent that turns on its own thread, so it keeps turning while
      the UI thread is blocked.
      Page building blocks: MaBodyScroll/MaPaneScroll scroll areas whose bar sits inside the right gutter
      (MaScrollArea.Gutter), MaList/MaRowList/MaTileList ItemsControl lists on MaStackPanel/MaTileGrid,
      MaListCard/MaRowCard/MaAccentCard/MaInsetCard cards, MaAccentBar/MaVeil/MaSidePane/MaStatusBar/
      MaDivider/MaCover borders, the MaStatValue text, MaTile.IsSelected for chosen tiles, MaAccentTile
      (a tile with a left bar in its own Accent) and MaPicker, a drop-down for choosing a person or login
      whose options show a name, a status light and a muted trailing text.
      MindAttic.Components.Wpf.Mvvm: ObservableObject, RelayCommand, CollectionSync (in-place
      ReorderTo/SyncBy) and ZoomLevel (80-200% with Ctrl+Plus/Minus/0). MaToolTips.KeepOpen makes
      tooltips stay up until dismissed, and MaHighContrast swaps the Windows high-contrast colours
      into every theme brush live. The palette meets WCAG 2.2 AA by itself: MaRec text is 4.5:1 and
      a text field's MaFieldBorder outline 3:1 on every surface. Light and dark themes: MaTheme.Set switches
      every control live between the dark default and a light palette at the same contrast standard (high
      contrast still wins), MaThemeToggle is the sun/moon switch, and MaWindow.ThemedTitleBar keeps the
      title bar in step.</Description>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Web.WebView2" Version="1.0.3179.45" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
